# Number Limits Check

## Setup

Evaluate this cell first to install Kino.

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:kino, "~> 0.19.0"}
])
```

## Order form

Evaluate this cell after setup. It renders an order form with a quantity
number input constrained to 1-10 (step 1, default 5) and live change reporting.

```elixir
form =
  Kino.Control.form(
    [
      quantity: Kino.Input.number("Quantity", min: 1, max: 10, step: 1, default: 5)
    ],
    submit: "Submit order",
    report_changes: true
  )

Kino.render(form)
```

## Status output

Evaluate this cell after the form cell. It shows a live status line below the form:
"No changes yet." until the first edit, then a draft line per reported change
and a saved line per submit.

```elixir
status = Kino.Frame.new()
Kino.render(status)
Kino.Frame.render(status, Kino.Markdown.new("No changes yet."))

Kino.listen(form, fn
  %{type: :change, data: data} ->
    Kino.Frame.render(status, Kino.Markdown.new("Draft: quantity #{data.quantity}"))

  %{type: :submit, data: data} ->
    Kino.Frame.render(status, Kino.Markdown.new("Saved: quantity #{data.quantity}"))
end)
```
